## Prerequisites

- Node.js 20+
- npm 10+
- Angular CLI (`npm install -g @angular/cli`)
{{ if model.manifest.ui_targets | array.contains "mobile" }}
- Capacitor CLI (`npm install -g @capacitor/cli`)
- Android Studio (for Android builds)
- Xcode (for iOS builds, macOS only)
{{ end }}

## Getting Started

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Create the runtime configuration (API URL and Cognito app client), then edit it
cp apps/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/src/assets/app-config.example.json apps/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/src/assets/app-config.json

# Start development server
npm start

# Open browser at http://localhost:4200
```

Sign-in uses Amazon Cognito (authorization code + PKCE). Without a valid `app-config.json` the app
starts with sign-in unavailable. See **[AUTHENTICATION.md](AUTHENTICATION.md)** for the Cognito
setup, configuration keys, token handling and tenancy rules.

